From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] c33: ptrace requests for the thread area

PTRACE_GET_THREAD_AREA and PTRACE_SET_THREAD_AREA (25 and 26) read and
write a stopped task's TLS base, as the C33 kernel provides them.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/sys/ptrace.h b/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/sys/ptrace.h
--- a/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/sys/ptrace.h
+++ b/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/sys/ptrace.h
@@ -103,6 +103,14 @@
   PTRACE_SYSCALL = 24,
 #define PT_SYSCALL PTRACE_SYSCALL
 
+#ifdef __c33__
+  /* Read/write the stopped task's TLS base at index zero. */
+  PTRACE_GET_THREAD_AREA = 25,
+#define PT_GET_THREAD_AREA PTRACE_GET_THREAD_AREA
+  PTRACE_SET_THREAD_AREA = 26,
+#define PT_SET_THREAD_AREA PTRACE_SET_THREAD_AREA
+#endif
+
   /* Set ptrace filter options.  */
   PTRACE_SETOPTIONS = 0x4200,
 #define PT_SETOPTIONS PTRACE_SETOPTIONS
